      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Let $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\}$ be a basis of ${R}^{2}$ and $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $B=\\{{b}_{1},{b}_{2}\\},$ where ${b}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2}$ and ${b}_{2}=2{c}_{1}?$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={c}_{1}+3{c}_{2} \\\\  & =3{c}_{2}+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 3(\\frac{1}{3}{c}_{2})+\\frac{1}{2}(2{c}_{1}) \\\\  & =9{b}_{1}+\\frac{1}{2}{b}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}].$",
